{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== FIXED, RED-FIRST, IN THE SAME CHANGE AS 727f. ===\n\nThe 727f fix did NOT already cover this — verified, not assumed. That suppression matched only\n`(outbound, update, field_drift)`; this defect is `(outbound, create, unbound_local)`, and the\nresurrect-create still emitted with it applied. So the suppression was generalised rather than\nreused: `reconcile_helpers.drop_snapshot_echo_field_updates` becomes\n`drop_snapshot_differ_local_state_emissions`, matching a `(direction, action, reason)` triple set\n\n    (\"outbound\", \"update\", \"field_drift\")    <- 727f\n    (\"outbound\", \"create\", \"unbound_local\")  <- this ticket\n\nplus a mandatory `provenance[\"source\"] == \"differ\"` conjunct so invariant-seeded mutations that\nreuse a reason string are never swept up. `differ.compute_mutations` is unmodified.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\n\n1. \"The experiment above is run and recorded before any code change.\" DONE — see the previous\n   comment. Result PREDICTED-TRUE: `client.create_issue` called once on pass 2 with fields\n   rebuilt from the stale prev summary.\n2. \"A key absent from the current snapshot but present in the previous one never reaches\n   `create_issue`, proven by a RED-first unit test.\" DONE, at two boundaries:\n   * `orchestrate/test_reconcile_once.py::test_a_key_absent_from_the_current_snapshot_never_reaches_create_issue`\n     — the live-path oracle, asserting at the TRANSPORT (`create_issue` recorded, must be never\n     called) precisely because both downstream guards were shown not to catch it.\n   * `diffing/test_snapshot_differ_stale_local_state.py::test_a_key_that_left_the_fetch_window_plans_no_outbound_create`\n     — the diff-phase oracle, with a fixture precondition asserting the raw differ really does\n     emit the `unbound_local` create so the cell cannot pass vacuously.\n   Both seen RED against origin/main with a failure message naming the mechanism, GREEN after.\n3. \"`differ.py:7-11` and `run_differs.py:205` are corrected so the module docstring stops\n   describing a contract the caller does not honour.\" DONE. `differ.py`'s module docstring now\n   carries a CAVEAT naming the unmigrated caller, which arms misfire there, and where the\n   compensation lives; `run_differs`'s docstring says the same from the caller's side. Both state\n   that migrating the caller and deleting the suppression must happen in the SAME change.\n\nMUTATION CHECK: removing `(\"outbound\",\"create\",\"unbound_local\")` from the suppressed set returns\nexactly this ticket's two oracles to RED with the resurrect message, while both 727f oracles stay\nGREEN — so the suppression is correctly scoped per arm, and each ticket's oracle really pins its\nown arm. No AttributeError / import-error style false mutation.\n\nCOMPLETENESS: fed a realistic fetched-snapshot pair, `compute_mutations` can emit exactly three\nthings — `jira_new` inbound create (correct here, preserved), `unbound_local` outbound create and\n`field_drift` outbound update (both suppressed). This ticket's observation that the remaining\nlocal_state-shaped arms are inert is CONFIRMED: `duplicate_local_id`, `ambiguous_local_binding`,\n`dangling_jira_local_id` and `_compute_mutations_emit_absent_partner_probes` never fire from a\nfetched snapshot, because they read `local_id` / `jira_key` fields such an entry never carries.\nSo no residual wrong emission is left at this call site.\n\nSTILL OPEN, DELIBERATELY NOT FIXED HERE — the section of this ticket headed \"the differ's\nlocal_state contract was never migrated\" describes a larger latent problem this change only\nDOCUMENTS: the `(inbound, probe)` dispatch chain (`run_differs`, `inbound_probe.py`,\n`backend.probe_remote`) still has no live producer, because its only producer is the unreachable\nabsent-partner loop. That is a missing capability, not this defect, and ADR 0028 para 2's\ndirect-GET confirmation path is where a deleted issue should actually be resolved. Worth its own\nticket rather than smuggling a new subsystem into a bug fix.\n\nGATES: `make lint` clean, `make typecheck` clean, `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` 1808 passed."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785687874302526001,"uuid":"1a2f1223-8dd6-45d2-a1a1-7acb7a9d9983"}